WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.400
PRESENTER: The first stretch
limousines, built around 1928,

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.115
usually transported big bands
and their musical equipment.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.240
Luxury sedans with
an extended chassis

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.240
are typically associated
with special occasions,

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.135
such as weddings, proms,
or night on the town.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:29.890
It takes about 475 hours
of work and painstaking

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:34.290
detail to transform a luxury
sedan into a stretch limo.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.990
Workers cut an
ordinary-sized car

00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:40.720
in half using cutting wheels.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.690
Before cutting begins,
the inside of the car

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:46.690
is stripped away, along with
other components such as

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:49.390
the gas tank and drive shaft.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:52.210
Workers cut away the
inner support structure

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:55.480
and cut across the floor of the
car with a reciprocating saw.

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:02.370
The car is now
completely cut in half.

00:01:04.769 --> 00:01:06.930
Workers wheel the
back half of the car

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.300
away from the front half.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.700
They place the back
half on the exact spot

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.705
where the limousine will
gradually be assembled.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.810
The construction
department employees

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.930
insert steel frame rails into
the front half of the car.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:31.830
They insert the rails on
both sides of the front half

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:34.650
before inserting the rails
into the back half of the car.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.440
They measure the
length of the frame

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.320
rails to make sure that
the frame is square

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.480
and that the two halves
are the correct distance

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.340
apart to build the limousine.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:53.580
A worker welds the rails
to the frames of the front

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.280
and back halves of
the original car.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:59.520
They position the drive shaft
tunnel, which houses the steel

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.220
drive shaft and exhaust
pipes, and weld it

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.780
to the original vehicle tunnel.

00:02:08.039 --> 00:02:12.390
They position the floor, which
is made of galvanized steel,

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:14.520
and weld it to the
frame rails and tunnel.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.860
They weld the steel
roof rails into place.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.360
They connect the new
rails to the roof

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.630
rails in the original vehicle.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:34.560
A worker welds a vertical
side post into place.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.650
With a level, he checks that
the post of hardened steel

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.175
is perfectly vertical before
welding the base of the post

00:02:41.175 --> 00:02:42.210
to the floor frame.

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.710
A roof panel made of galvanized
steel is put in place.

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.770
Workers install the
limousine's bar.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.960
They've already installed
the steel seat frames.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.230
Next, they install an outer body
panel complete with a hardened

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:04.310
steel crash bar.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:08.210
They screw the panel into place.

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:11.450
The screws will be removed
once the panel has bonded

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:13.280
solidly to the limousine frame.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:18.650
A worker sprays on
three coats of paint

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:21.230
then applies two coats of
protective clear coating.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.260
Once the painting
process is complete,

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:30.155
workers install the
laminated safety side glass.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.150
Another worker
sprays contact cement

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:39.410
on the roof of the limousine in
preparation for the vinyl top.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:43.130
He stretches the vinyl across
the roof and, with his hand,

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:46.730
presses the fabric
down into the crevices,

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:48.875
then he carefully
trims off the excess.

00:03:51.590 --> 00:03:53.570
He presses a strip
of chrome molding

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.400
into place on the
top of the vinyl.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.650
Workers in the
interior department

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:05.900
install the back of a leather
seat and a leather bench seat.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:12.110
After reupholstering the
original rear seat to match,

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.150
they return it to
its original spot

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.971
in the back of the limousine.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.560
A systems installer connects
the electrical systems

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:24.800
for the control center located
behind the driver's seat.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.790
A panel lists relays and fuses.

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:31.550
The original center console
is then reinstalled.

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:37.470
A worker installs a video
monitor in the limousine.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.310
Next, he rolls out
the floor mats.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.675
The acrylic disco bar
lighting system is tested.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:54.750
In just 21 days, the
original car is transformed

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.120
into a luxurious limousine.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.520
With test drives and
quality control checks

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.280
complete, enjoy a ride
in the lap of luxury.

